# _template.kv — 知识图谱条目模板
# 用法: 复制此文件为 E605.kv，填写各字段
# 对应的人类文档: doc/E605.md
#
# 格式规则:
#   - key: value（冒号后一个空格，value 到行尾）
#   - 多行值: 下一行以空格开头 = 续行
#   - 列表值: 逗号分隔
#   - 正则值: | 分隔多个模式
#   - 以 # 开头的行为注释
#   - 空行忽略
#====================================================================

# ═══ Layer 0: 错误面 (Error Surface) ═══
# trigger_tool: 出错的工具 (configure/cmake/meson/make/gcc/clang/ld/python/pip/install/test/runtime)
# phase:         出错阶段 (configuration/compilation/linking/installation/testing/runtime)
# error_signature: 正则表达式(|分隔), 用于精确匹配日志文本
id:                     E605
trigger_tool:           meson|test|runtime
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        cannot execute binary file|Exec format error|exit status 77|TIMEOUT.*killed by signal 15|Could not configure.*build.dat|TLS support is not available|GDummyTlsBackend|Could not connect to 127\.0\.0\.1: Connection refused|Error loading shared library.*\.so

# ═══ Layer 1: 识别层 (Recognition) ═══
# severity:      3=🔴blocking  2=🟡medium  1=🟢minor  0=✅resolved
# category:      分类标签（受控词表 64 词，逗号分隔，最多 5 个；add/promote 自动归一化）
# prescan_pattern: （可选）预编译源码扫描正则——写入后 PreScanner 运行时自动派生
#                   PSCAN-KB-{id} 规则，无需改 pre-scan-rules.yaml（知识增长即扫描能力增长）
# prescan_globs:   （可选）扫描范围 glob 列表，默认 '*.c, *.h, *.cc, *.cpp, *.sh, Makefile*, *.mk'
# 词表: platform, compat, limitation, detection, hmdfs, ohos, selinux, kernel, portability, libc, musl, posix, syscall, headers, threading, socket, network, build-system, cmake, autotools ...（全表见 scripts/ohc/kb_taxonomy.py）
# match_keywords: 纯文本关键词(逗号分隔), 用于粗筛(固定字符串匹配F)
# title:         简短标题(一句话描述错误模式)
severity:               2
category:               testing, network, meson, ohos, build-system
match_keywords:         cross build, aarch64, OHOS, Exec format error, exit status 77, Meson test, external HTTP, TIMEOUT, deterministic fixture, GDummyTlsBackend, TLS support is not available, loopback connection refused, server readiness, test_package runtime closure, loader-first stage, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, transitive SONAME
title: Cross-built OHOS test binaries require a native host harness and bounded fixtures

# ═══ Layer 2: 诊断层 (Diagnosis) ═══
# root_cause:       一句话根因描述(逗号可分行)
# affected_scope:   影响范围
# verification_cmd: 验证诊断是否正确的命令
root_cause: A Meson test directory generated by an OHOS/aarch64 cross build contains target ELF executables that WSL/Linux x86_64 cannot execute, so Meson reports exit status 77 or Exec format error before any assertion runs. Legacy upstream tests may call an external HTTPS service; a native target without a GIO TLS backend reports GDummyTlsBackend before request assertions. Even a loopback test is nondeterministic when it spawns a raw server thread without a readiness handshake. After packaging, Conan's run environment may omit component-backed transitive directories, and some native OHOS loaders still fail to reach indirect SONAMEs in later entries of a printed long LD_LIBRARY_PATH. Treating any of these outcomes as PASS hides an unexecuted or indeterminate test.
affected_scope: Cross-compiled C/C++ libraries whose upstream test runner emits target executables, especially Meson/GLib suites containing network-backed tests and Conan test packages that consume shared libraries with transitive component dependencies. A test-only loopback fixture applies when the original test validates request construction and response parsing rather than the public service's TLS implementation, and when the same test registration, requests, payload shape, parsing and assertions are retained.
verification_cmd: PYTHONPATH=<task>/meson-runtime python3 -m mesonbuild.mesonmain test -C <task>/host-native-build --no-rebuild --print-errorlogs --num-processes 2; verify the summary is N/N PASS with skipped=0, timeout=0, and hash-bind the raw log and fixture request log

# ═══ Layer 3: 方案层 (Solution Space) ★ ═══
# 推荐方案 (priority 越小越优先, 从 1 开始)
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           native-host-test-with-private-fixture
rec_description:        Build the same upstream tests natively in a task-owned prefix. When the target has no GIO TLS backend, replace only external HTTPS transport with a loopback HTTP fixture while preserving assertions. Start every loopback service through one readiness-signalled ephemeral-port helper. For the packaged consumer, independently enumerate the tested package plus all host transitive component libdirs, materialize every validated SONAME into one conflict-checked loader-first directory, self-sign critical copied roots at their final native path, and retain conanrun.
rec_command:            meson setup <host-build> <host-source> -Dtests=true && meson compile -C <host-build> -j2 && meson test -C <host-build> --no-rebuild --print-errorlogs --num-processes 2
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:               source-copy-fixture

# 回退方案 (当推荐方案不可用时尝试)
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      bounded-network-retry
fallback_description:   Retry the original endpoint once with an explicit short timeout only when reachability is known to be transient and a real TLS backend is present; otherwise record the failure and use the bounded loopback fixture path.
fallback_command:       curl --connect-timeout 8 --max-time 15 <endpoint>
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

# ★ 禁止策略 (与推荐方案同等重要) ★
# forbid_N_pattern:     正则(|分隔), 匹配则拒绝/警告
# forbid_N_reason:      为什么禁止
# forbid_N_consequence: 违反后的后果
forbid_1_pattern:       mark.*exit status 77.*PASS|skip.*as.*pass|ignore.*TIMEOUT
forbid_1_reason:        A skipped target binary or a timed-out network call does not execute the assertions.
forbid_1_consequence:   The denominator becomes unverifiable and Pre-PR may accept an untested package.
forbid_2_pattern:       reuse.*target.*binary.*host|install.*fixture.*package|skip.*flickr|fixture.*proves.*TLS
forbid_2_reason:        A test fixture may replace only unavailable external transport; it must not enter the installed package, remove the test, or be presented as TLS coverage.
forbid_2_consequence:   Package semantics drift, the upstream denominator shrinks, or transport coverage is overstated.
# forbid_2_pattern:
# forbid_2_reason:
# forbid_2_consequence:

